Why Is Demand Increasing
Serialization Regulations: DSCSA, EU requirements, and national serialization mandates are pushing pharmaceutical manufacturers toward package-level identification and traceability.
Counterfeit Drug Prevention: Track and trace systems help authenticate medicines, prevent diversion, and improve supply-chain security.
Digital Supply Chains: EPCIS, enterprise software, aggregation, machine vision, and cloud connectivity are transforming pharmaceutical traceability into an integrated digital infrastructure.

Pharma Track and Trace Watch: From Serialization to End-to-End Traceability
Pharmaceutical traceability is moving beyond packaging-line serialization toward connected supply-chain networks. Modern systems combine DataMatrix codes, RFID, aggregation, enterprise software, verification, EPCIS data exchange, and exception management to provide visibility from manufacturing through distribution and dispensing.

